  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Unsettled weather returns Friday night and Saturday, \nfollowed by improving conditions Saturday night and Sunday.\n\nAfter one more dry and warm day on Friday...conditions will turn \nmore unsettled for Friday night and Saturday as deep-layer ridging \nover our area gives way to a low-amplitude mid-level trough and \nassociated surface low sliding across Ontario and Quebec...with the \nlatter slowly pushing its trailing cold front through the area \nbetween Saturday afternoon and evening.\n\nAn initial shot of DCVA coupled with increasing moisture along the \nfront flank of the approaching trough will lead to an increasing \npotential for showers...and perhaps an isolated thunderstorm across \nfar WNY later Friday night. Better chances for showers and scattered \nthunderstorms may then follow on Saturday with approach/passage of a \npre-frontal trough and the cold front itself...with convective \npotential likely to be maximized along and inland from developing \nlake breeze boundaries. \n\nWith PWATs climbing to between 1.5 and 1.75 inches any storms that \ndevelop on Saturday could produce locally heavy rainfall...though \nwith the dry antecedent conditions of late these would be unlikely \nto pose hydro issues unless any training of cells is realized. \nGenerally modest to locally moderate instability coupled with deep-\nlayer shear of 30-40 knots could also lead to a few isolated \nstronger storms capable of locally strong gusty winds and hail \nSaturday afternoon and evening...with the greatest risk for such \ncurrently looking to lie across the western Southern Tier. That \nsaid...the better severe risk on Saturday looks to be to our south \nand west over the upper Ohio Valley...where a greater reservoir of \ninstability looks to be in place. \n\nConvection will then wind down from west to east Saturday night\nwith the frontal passage and loss of heating. Lingering \ntroughing may then lead to another couple showers/an isolated \nstorm across far eastern portions of the area on Sunday...with \nmainly dry weather otherwise prevailing.",
